id: pm-9rgaal
title: "Outcome milestone: SDK-complete core — every CLI and MCP capability reachable from the public pm SDK"
description: "Outcome milestone for completing the public SDK boundary: every CLI and MCP capability is implemented through documented public SDK primitives, with presentation layers containing no domain logic."
type: Milestone
status: open
priority: 1
tags[6]: "horizon:near-mid",milestone,outcome,platform,sdk,universal-tool
created_at: "2026-07-24T23:43:03.056Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-03T06:42:45.724Z"
deadline: "2026-12-31T00:00:00.000Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 6000
acceptance_criteria: "SDK import-boundary baseline is zero and the ratchet is a hard failing gate, not an allowlist; Every remaining promotion slice under pm-usfg is closed with public exports and authoring docs; A published exemplar package implements a complete workflow using only public SDK exports, with no local shim; CLI and MCP handlers contain argument parsing, rendering, and no domain logic, proven by a structural test"
goal: sdk-complete-core
objective: The CLI and MCP server contain presentation logic only; every primitive they use is public SDK surface
value: "The SDK is the product's leverage point: anything not in it cannot be reused, embedded, or extended by third parties."
impact: "Unblocks the universal-platform milestone, the conformance gate for external packages, and any embedding of pm in another runtime."
outcome: The private-core import baseline is zero and hard-gated; a non-trivial third-party surface is buildable against published SDK exports alone.
why_now: Every new command shipped against private core widens the promotion backlog; the boundary ratchet only holds if the remaining slices land.
parent: pm-doxj
risk: medium
confidence: high
